      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Exact angiographic and identification of significant stenosis of the left main coronary artery is imperative prior to performing elective percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. A patient is presented with an apparent angiographically significant, but physiologically insignificant, left main stenosis. Both angiographic and physiological methods of detecting \"false positive and negative\" left main stenoses are discussed."},
